NOTICE — BRISQUE model redistribution (model/other_models/brisque_live.model)
============================================================================

This directory ships `brisque_live.model`, the trained libsvm EPSILON_SVR model
used by the fork's BRISQUE no-reference image-quality extractor
(core/src/feature/brisque.c, feature name "brisque"). The model and its
companion feature range-normalization arrays originate from the LIVE laboratory
at The University of Texas at Austin and the BRISQUE authors' reference
implementations. The fork redistributes the model under a documented
research-use attribution exception (see docs/adr/1115-brisque-nr-metric.md).

Required citation
-----------------
Any use of this model must cite the originating publication:

  A. Mittal, A. K. Moorthy and A. C. Bovik, "No-Reference Image Quality
  Assessment in the Spatial Domain," IEEE Transactions on Image Processing,
  vol. 21, no. 12, pp. 4695-4708, Dec. 2012. doi:10.1109/TIP.2012.2214050.
  https://live.ece.utexas.edu/publications/2012/TIP%20BRISQUE.pdf

Provenance
----------
- Trained model (allmodel, native libsvm text format):
    svm_type epsilon_svr, kernel_type rbf, gamma 0.05, nr_class 2,
    total_sv 770, rho -155.845, probA 6.34795.
  Obtained from the BRISQUE reference C++ implementation mirror:
    https://github.com/krshrimali/No-Reference-Image-Quality-Assessment-using-BRISQUE-Model
    (path C++/allmodel) — a verbatim copy of the original LIVE-lab model also
    distributed via gregfreeman/image_quality_toolbox (+brisque/allmodel), the
    MATLAB pipeline that trained it.
  sha256 = 19526fb799c4c7992ccc109fcfecddb25976ba024b194cd3ee275d27e8909c8d
  bytes  = 351414

- Feature range arrays (min_[36] / max_[36], libsvm svm-scale [-1, 1]):
    Baked directly into core/src/feature/brisque.c. These are the INLINE arrays
    from the reference computescore.cpp prediction path (the array the trained
    model expects), NOT the separate C++/allrange file — which is a different,
    prediction-inconsistent set the reference code never reads (ADR-1115,
    docs/metrics/brisque.md "Range arrays").

